######################Git revert#############

1. Git Revert (Step-by-Step)
Reverting is used to undo a specific commit by creating a new "inverse" commit.

Step 1: Initialize a repository and create a file

Bash
git init revert-demo
cd revert-demo
echo "Version 1: Initial Content" > file.txt
git add file.txt
git commit -m "First commit"
Step 2: Make a "bad" change and commit it

Bash
echo "Version 2: This change is a mistake!" >> file.txt
git add file.txt
git commit -m "Added bad feature"
Step 3: Identify the Commit ID to undo

Bash
git log --oneline
(You will see a list. Note the 7-character ID next to "Added bad feature", e.g., a1b2c3d)

Step 4: Execute the Revert

Bash
git revert a1b2c3d
(A text editor will open asking for a commit message. Save and close it—usually Ctrl+X then Y then Enter in Nano, or :wq in Vim).

Step 5: Verify the result

Bash
cat file.txt
git log --oneline


#################git conflict###################

2. Git Conflict (Step-by-Step)
A conflict happens when the same line is changed in two different branches.

Step 1: Setup the repository and main branch

Bash
git init conflict-demo
cd conflict-demo
echo "Base Title" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "Main title added"
Step 2: Create a new branch and change the line

Bash
git checkout -b feature-branch
echo "Feature Title" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "Updated title on feature branch"
Step 3: Switch back to main and change the SAME line

Bash
git checkout main
echo "Main Title Update" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "Updated title on main branch"
Step 4: Try to merge (This triggers the conflict)

Bash
git merge feature-branch
(Terminal will output: CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in index.html)

Step 5: Resolve the conflict manually
Open index.html in a text editor. You will see:

HTML
<<<<<<< HEAD
Main Title Update
=======
Feature Title
>>>>>>> feature-branch
Delete the markers (<<<<, ====, >>>>).

Keep the text you want (e.g., change it to "Final Title").

Step 6: Finish the merge

Bash
git add index.html
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict manually"


